Keep Tracy's rpmalloc regions out of transparent huge pages.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    Tracy constructs its profiler at static init, even with `TRACY_ON_DEMAND`,
    and its rpmalloc maps large sparse regions for the serial queues and
    per-thread queue blocks. With `transparent_hugepage=always` the first
    touch of each region faults in a whole 2 MiB page, so an idle server or
    client with no profiler attached kept about 8 MiB of untouched queue
    memory resident.

WHAT STAYS AVAILABLE
    The mappings are unchanged. Only `MADV_NOHUGEPAGE` is applied when
    rpmalloc was not asked for huge pages, so a connected capture behaves as
    upstream with 4 KiB faults.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    `scripts/vendor-tree.sh tracy` fails during configure. Re-point the hunk at
    the Linux `mmap` branch of `_rpmalloc_mmap_os`. Do not edit
    `mono.vendor/tracy` in place.

--- a/public/client/tracy_rpmalloc.cpp
+++ b/public/client/tracy_rpmalloc.cpp
@@ -908,6 +908,11 @@
 		}
 	}
 #    endif
+#    if defined(MADV_NOHUGEPAGE)
+	// Keep sparse profiler buffers at 4 KiB granularity under THP=always.
+	if (ptr && ptr != MAP_FAILED && !_memory_huge_pages)
+		madvise(ptr, size + padding, MADV_NOHUGEPAGE);
+#    endif
 	_rpmalloc_set_name(ptr, size + padding);
 #  elif defined(MAP_ALIGNED)
 	const size_t align = (sizeof(size_t) * 8) - (size_t)(__builtin_clzl(size - 1));
